    {
      "id": "20261008T070348Z-d6e2e0bb#1",
      "line": 50,
      "path": "reports/20261008-development-replay-parallel-acceptance/README.md",
      "rule": "R11",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "The README says the validator refuses four independent mutations after their digests are rebound, but the commit keeps no check that does this, and `validate.py` reads only the fixed `ROOT`, so it cannot run on a changed copy (earlier reports keep a `check_mutations.py` for this). Fix: Add a `check_mutations.py` that copies the report and refuses the four mutations, and let `validate` take the report root as an argument."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261008T070348Z-d6e2e0bb#2",
      "line": 11,
      "path": "reports/20261008-development-replay-parallel-acceptance/acceptance.json",
      "rule": "R11",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "`validate.py` never reads `acceptance.json`, so wrong summary values (phase seconds, outer seconds, storage device, fixture count, flags) still pass the check. Fix: In `validate.py`, compare each field of `acceptance.json` with the original receipts and reports for both platforms."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261008T070348Z-d6e2e0bb#3",
      "line": 19,
      "path": "reports/20261008-development-replay-parallel-acceptance/validate.py",
      "rule": "R9",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "The docstring of `read_original` says it parses a file only after its compressed and original bytes verify, but the function checks no digest and depends on `validate` checking first. Fix: Check the digest in `read_original`, or change the docstring to say that the caller must verify the bytes first."
    }
